cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this result, please cite it as below."
title: "An explicit lower bound in Turán's pure power sum problem"
abstract: >-
  An explicit form of A. Biró's lower bound (Indag. Math. (N.S.) 11 (2000), 343-358) in Turán's pure power
  sum problem (Erdős problem #519; constant C42 of the Optimization Constants repository): R_n > 1/2 +
  2^(-32176926823186696) for every n, hence R_n > 1/2 + 10^(-10^16). The method is Biró's; his constants are
  made explicit and the final inequalities are verified in Arb ball arithmetic. Unrefereed; made with
  substantial help from an AI model (Claude Opus 5.5, Anthropic).
